                <pb facs="0603" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg519"/>

                <head>No. 268.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Presson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Custom-House, Gloucester, Mass.</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Collector’s Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-08-10"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 10, 1886</date>.
                        [Received August 11.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your telegram of 5th instant I
                    inclose affidavits of Captain Cunningham, of schooner Rattler, and his passenger
                    and crew, in relation to their treatment at Shelburne, Nova Scotia, on going in
                    there for shelter on 3d instant.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>D. S. PEESSON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Collector.</hi></signed></closer>



